        "anonymized": false,
        "avatarURL": "https://canny-assets.io/images/44e612f9a18494f1e08ec0798cd64966.png",
        "created": "2025-04-14T23:12:19.670Z",
        "name": "pico㌰poco",
        "serviceAccount": false,
        "urlName": "<redacted>"
      },
      "authorID": null,
      "boardID": "58c62f2b3cf8f8367753b2f0",
      "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
      "created": "2025-06-06T11:03:01.131Z",
      "deleted": false,
      "deletedAt": null,
      "fileURLs": [],
      "files": [],
      "imageURLs": [],
      "integrationSourceType": null,
      "internal": false,
      "itemSourceType": null,
      "mentionedUserIDs": null,
      "mentionedUsers": [],
      "mergeID": null,
      "parentID": "67fd9d3612dea558cc4ba147",
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "601acb21f76d3163c5e74920",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "restoredAt": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "After that, I conducted various experiments on my own. It seems that the issue is definitely related to IPv6 processing. In the PICO4 standalone, there are no settings to disalbe IPv6, but the problem was RESOLVED by routing through a server that blocks IPv6. More specifically, I created a local DNS and routed through it. This method is not a solution that anyone can easily implement, but I believe it proves that the issue was indeed caused by IPv6. I have not confirmed any other drawbacks from using this method. Therefore, I would like to suggest the developers to consider making a fix based on this approach.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
